---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Mental Skills for Athletes: Visualization, Focus, Self-Talk, Routines"
  description="Practical mental skills techniques for athletes: visualization, focus, self-talk, routines, and mental toughness to improve performance."
  ogImage="/images/basketball-focus-routine.webp"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Mental Skills</p>
      <h1>Mental Skills for Athletic Performance</h1>
      <p>Practical, research-backed techniques athletes use to build focus, confidence, and consistency.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p>Mental skills are trainable, just like physical skills. Visualization helps athletes rehearse successful performance. Structured self-talk replaces doubt with constructive cues. Pre-performance routines create consistency under pressure. Focus training teaches athletes to direct attention where it matters most.</p>
      <p>Our technique guides will walk through each skill step by step, with examples athletes actually use. Everything here is educational content about performance skills, not clinical advice. See our <a href="/what-is-sports-psychology/">overview of sports psychology</a> for the foundations.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
